WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.343
Build a simple side table with Rectangle,
Push/Pull, Make Object, Move, and Move Copy.

00:00:07.343 --> 00:00:15.043
Choose Rectangle. Pick opposite corners to draw
a tabletop sixty centimeters wide and deep.

00:00:15.043 --> 00:00:22.886
Choose Push/Pull, select the face, and pull it
upward. Type three for the tabletop thickness.

00:00:22.886 --> 00:00:30.514
Select the tabletop geometry and choose Make
Object. This keeps it separate from the legs.

00:00:30.514 --> 00:00:38.357
With Move, lift the tabletop forty-two centimeters.
Its upper surface is now forty-five high.

00:00:38.357 --> 00:00:46.914
Draw a four-centimeter square below a corner. Pull
it up forty-two centimeters, then make it an object.

00:00:46.914 --> 00:00:54.543
Use Move Copy to make a second leg. Select
both legs and copy them across to the far side.

00:00:54.543 --> 00:01:02.886
The table is complete: one top and four linked legs.
Save the project, then explore your own design.
